From 4577d73133b8dc2aa94dda49af9665c9374d3fb8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 13:41:11 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: DomD's join and typed passphrases in the relay and
 DomaWifiRelay

DomA's station joins the shadow BSS within seconds whatever happens to
the real AP, so the Wi-Fi screen showed a network as joined while DomD
was still looking for it, dropped it without a reason when DomD failed,
and took any typed passphrase as connected until DomD's answer.

doma-wifi-relay now:
- writes DomD's join to relay.state: "pending" after each connect it
  forwards, "offline:<reason>" (not-found, wrong-key, rejected,
  timeout, error) for DomD's FAILED, "offline:retry" while a later
  connect for the SSID is pending, "offline:lost" for LOST, and the
  app's token (psk#<hex>) as a fourth field on every line that answers
  a request with one;
- marks the connect for a typed passphrase ,"kind":"u", so that DomD's
  agent answers its WRONG_KEY at once when the SSID has never been
  COMPLETED with it, and puts the passphrase into the shadow row only
  once DomD has joined with it (its COMPLETED, or a BACK after a
  timed-out join; "online" once hostapd beacons it);
- times its intervals by /proc/uptime instead of mksh's $SECONDS (the
  wall clock, which NTP steps once DomA's network is validated), counts
  every hostapd restart for BOUNCE_MIN_S except one while hostapd
  beacons only the hidden idle BSS, and holds restarts for the list
  while the app is about to join the BSS of an "online" (30 s at most).
  doma_shadow_ap may read proc_uptime.

DomaWifiRelay now:
- shows one notification for DomD's join (connecting, connected, cannot
  connect with the reason, disconnected); a failure opens the Wi-Fi
  settings on a tap;
- connects a typed passphrase's network on the "online" with its token,
  once a scan sees the restarted shadow BSS, keeping its auto-join off
  meanwhile; on a wrong-key answer it connects once so that the screen
  asks for the password;
- keeps the (SSID, passphrase) pairs DomD refused as HMAC-SHA-256 in
  device-protected storage and does not send them again after a boot;
- takes down the framework's "Failed to connect" (42) that the local
  handshake against the placeholder, and its own connect after a
  refusal, make it post.

xenvm_trout_rpi4_arm64/doma-wifi-relay.sh, sepolicy/doma_shadow_ap.te
and DomaWifiRelay/ become the same files as the Raspberry Pi 5's relay
and sepolicy and the doma-common DomaWifiRelay of AGL's meta-rpi-sodev.

On a Raspberry Pi 4 (2026-11-09, a WPA2 AP) a wrong passphrase was
told 13 s after the tap and not sent again after a reboot, and the
right one reached CONNECTED 25.6 s after the tap with one hostapd
restart.

